title: 'Migrate `pallet-sassafras` from the deprecated `ValidateUnsigned` trait to `#[pallet::authorize]`'

doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-sassafras` no longer uses the deprecated `ValidateUnsigned` trait and the
    `#[pallet::validate_unsigned]` attribute. The validation of `submit_tickets` moved to a
    `#[pallet::authorize]` callback.

    The validation semantics do not change. The callback rejects a call from
    `TransactionSource::External`, it rejects a call made after the first half of the epoch, and it
    builds the same transaction validity as before.

    Two changes affect a runtime that includes this pallet. The `Config` supertrait changed from
    `CreateBare<Call<Self>>` to `CreateAuthorizedTransaction<Call<Self>>`, and the runtime must put
    `frame_system::AuthorizeCall` in its transaction extension pipeline. `submit_tickets` now needs
    an authorized origin.

    `submit_tickets_unsigned_extrinsic` keeps its name, because it is a runtime API method and the
    `_unsigned_extrinsic` suffix is shared with `BabeApi`, `GrandpaApi` and `BeefyApi`. Only its
    documentation changed.

crates:
- name: pallet-sassafras
  bump: major
- name: sp-consensus-sassafras
  bump: patch
